meter_explanation": {"score": 4, "reasoning": "The uri parameter is explained as the URI to delete and is accompanied by a helpful example format. The source code confirms it handles URI parsing and path validation correctly."}, "length_completeness": {"score": 4, "reasoning": "The description spans multiple paragraphs covering purpose, warnings, arguments, return values, and examples. It is detailed and substantive without being overly verbose."}, "examples": {"score": 5, "reasoning": "Provides two concrete, realistic usage examples illustrating how to invoke delete_memory with valid domain-prefixed URIs."}}, "error_detail": null, "source_code_sha256": "21327f07a422480c3cf8fc88b0088ceafb93ec8d70ad838a33d1a2cd646a014a", "usage": {"input_tokens": 10104, "output_tokens": 380, "cache_read_input_tokens": 0, "cache_creation_input_tokens": 0}, "latency_ms": 2333.5447090212256, "evaluated_at": "2026-09-09T21:56:59.712815+00:00"}
{"schema_version": "1.0", "prompt_version": "v2", "tool_uid": "AGI-is-going-to-arrive/Memory-Palace::add_alias::backend/mcp_server.py:5441", "repo": {"name_with_owner": "AGI-is-going-to-arrive/Memory-Palace", "stargazer_count": 311, "primary_language": "Python"}, "tool": {"name": "add_alias", "qualified_name": "add_alias", "description": "Creates an alias URI pointing to the same memory as target_uri.\n\n    Use this to increase a memory's reachability via multiple URIs.\n    Aliases can even cross domains (e.g., link a writer draft to a core memory).\n\n    Args:\n        new_uri: New URI to create (alias)\n        target_uri: Existing URI to alias\n        priority: Retrieval priority for this specific alias context (lower = higher priority). This controls retrieval ordering for the alias.\n        disclosure: Disclosure condition for this specific alias context\n\n    Returns:\n        Success message\n\n    Examples:\n        add_alias(\"core://timeline/2024/05/20\", \"core://agent/my_user/first_meeting\", priority=1, disclosure=\"When I want to know how we start\")"}, "scenario": "with_source", "judge": {"id": "gemini-3.5-flash-lite", "provider": "google", "model_id": "gemini-3.5-flash-lite", "raw_model_version": "gemini-3.5-flash-lite"}, "status": "ok", "scores": {"purpose": {"score": 5, "reasoning": "The description clearly explains that the tool creates an alias URI pointing to an existing memory target, expanding reachability across domains."}, "guidelines": {"score": 3, "reasoning": "It explains when to use the tool (to increase reachability or cross domains), but provides minimal operational instructions beyond listing the parameters."}, "limitations": {"score": 2, "reasoning": "The description does not mention important constraints revealed in the code, such as that the target path must exist, parent directories for the new path must exist, or that certain domains like 'system://' are read-only."}, "parameter_explanation": {"score": 4, "reasoning": "Parameters like priority and disclosure are explained regarding their effect on context and retrieval ordering, though specific type constraints (like priority needing to be an integer >= 0) are omitted."}, "length_completeness": {"score": 4, "reasoning": "The description is thorough, containing a summary, use cases, argument descriptions, return value, and an example, satisfying most length and detail requirements."}, "examples": {"score": 5, "reasoning": "A clear, valid example call is provided demonstrating proper usage with positional URIs and keyword arguments for priority and disclosure."}}, "error_detail": null, "source_code_sha256": "9e9df1efdd455991db64cef60302e8482250e3567077641ec10b0b439b6a6291", "usage": {"input_tokens": 10015, "output_tokens": 335, "cache_read_input_tokens": 0, "cache_creation_input_tokens": 0}, "latency_ms": 2122.797958087176, "evaluated_at": "2026-09-09T21:57:01.764670+00:00"}
{"schema_version": "1.0", "prompt_version": "v2", "tool_uid": "AGI-is-going-to-arrive/Memory-Palace::search_memory::backend/mcp_server.py:5552", "repo": {"name_with_owner": "AGI-is-going-to-arrive/Memory-Palace", "stargazer_count": 311, "primary_language": "Python"}, "tool": {"name": "search_memory", "qualified_name": "search_memory", "description": "Search memories using keyword/semantic/hybrid retrieval.\n\n    Args:\n        query: Search query text.\n        mode: keyword / semantic / hybrid. Default from env or keyword.\n        max_results: Final number of returned items.\n        candidate_multiplier: Controls candidate pool before final top-k.\n        include_session: Whether to run session-first queue merge before global results.\n        filters: Optional object with:\n            - domain: domain scope\n            - path_prefix: path prefix scope\n            - max_priority: keep priority <= max_priority\n            - updated_after: ISO datetime filter (e.g. 2026-01-31T12:00:00Z)\n            - interaction_tier: fast/deep routing policy for search orchestration\n        scope_hint: Optional query-side scope hint (domain/path prefix/URI prefix).\n        verbose: When false, omit high-noise debug metadata fields from the response.\n\n    Returns:\n        Structured JSON string.\n\n    Examples:\n        search_memory(\"job\")\n        search_memory(\n            \"chapter arc\",\n            mode=\"hybrid\",\n            max_results=8,\n            include_session=True,\n            filters={\"domain\": \"writer\", \"path_prefix\": \"chapter_1\"}\n        )"}, "scenario": "description_only", "judge": {"id": "gemini-3.5-flash-lite", "provider": "google", "model_id": "gemini-3.5-flash-lite", "raw_model_version": "gemini-3.5-flash-lite"}, "status": "ok", "scores": {"purpose": {"score": 5, "reasoning": "The description clearly explains that the tool searches memories using keyword, semantic, or hybrid retrieval methods, covering its core functionality thoroughly."}, "guidelines": {"score": 3, "reasoning": "It specifies operational instructions through parameters like mode and filters, but lacks explicit decision-making activation criteria for when an agent should choose this tool over others."}, "limitations": {"score": 1, "reasoning": "There are no known constraints, caveats, or potential failure modes mentioned in the description."}, "parameter_explanation": {"score": 4, "reasoning": "The parameters like query, mode, max_results, include_session, filters, and scope_hint are well explained regarding their roles and options, though some minor schema details for nested filter properties could be richer."}, "length_completeness": {"score": 4, "reasoning": "The description is thorough and spans multiple lines of substantive detail covering function definition, arguments, return type, and examples, though it falls short of being an exhaustive prose essay."}, "examples": {"score": 4, "reasoning": "Provides two clear examples of correct usage, including a simple query and a more complex one utilizing parameters like mode, max_results, include_session, and filters."}}, "error_detail": null, "source_code_sha256": null, "usage": {"input_tokens": 1101, "output_tokens": 336, "cache_read_input_tokens": 0, "cache_creation_input_tokens": 0}, "latency_ms": 6574.4774581398815, "evaluated_at": "2026-09-09T21:57:06.288383+00:00"}
{"schema_version": "1.0", "prompt_version": "v2", "tool_uid": "AGI-is-going-to-arrive/Memory-Palace::read_memory::backend/mcp_server.py:4294", "repo": {"name_with_owner": "AGI-is-going-to-arrive/Memory-Palace", "stargazer_count": 311, "primary_language": "Python"}, "tool": {"name": "read_memory", "qualified_name": "read_memory", "description": "Reads a memory by its URI.\n\n    This is your primary mechanism for accessing memories.\n\n    Special System URIs:\n    - system://boot   : [Startup Only] Loads your core memories.\n    - system://index  : Loads a full index of all available memories.\n    - system://index-lite : Loads gist-backed lightweight index summary.\n    - system://audit  : Loads consolidated observability/audit summary.\n    - system://recent : Shows recently modified memories (default: 10).\n    - system://recent/N : Shows the N most recently modified memories (e.g. system://recent/20).\n\n    Note: Same Memory ID = same content (alias). Different ID + similar content = redundant content.\n\n    Args:\n        uri: The memory URI (e.g., \"core://memory-palace\", \"system://boot\")\n        chunk_id: Optional chunk index for partial reads (0-based).\n        range: Optional char range (`start:end` or `start-end`).\n        max_chars: Optional hard cap for returned characters.\n        include_ancestors: Optional parent-chain expansion for non-system URIs.\n\n    Returns:\n        - Default (no chunk/range/max_chars): legacy formatted memory text.\n        - Partial-read mode: structured JSON string with selection metadata.\n\n    Examples:\n        read_memory(\"core://agent\")\n        read_memory(\"core://agent/my_user\")\n        read_memory(\"writer://chapter_1/scene_1\")"}, "scenario": "description_only", "judge": {"id": "gemini-3.5-flash-lite", "provider": "google", "model_id": "gemini-3.5-flash-lite", "raw_model_version": "gemini-3.5-flash-lite"}, "status": "ok", "scores": {"purpose": {"score": 5, "reasoning": "The description clearly explains that the tool reads a memory by its URI and serves as the primary mechanism for accessing memories, including detailed descriptions of special system URIs."}, "guidelines": {"score": 4, "reasoning": "It specifies when to use the tool (e.g., startup via system://boot, listing via system://index) and explains how to invoke partial reads and parent-chain expansions, though step-by-step workflow instructions are slightly sparse."}, "limitations": {"score": 1, "reasoning": "There are no known constraints, failure modes, error conditions, or corner cases mentioned in the description."}, "parameter_explanation": {"score": 4, "reasoning": "Parameters like uri, chunk_id, range, max_chars, and include_ancestors are well-described with explanations of their roles and formats."}, "length_completeness": {"score": 5, "reasoning": "The description is thorough, spanning multiple substantive paragraphs covering system URIs, arguments, return formats, and examples."}, "examples": {"score": 3, "reasoning": "It provides basic usage examples showing function calls with various URIs, but does not show expected outputs or complex usage involving parameters like range or chunk_id."}}, "error_detail": null, "source_code_sha256": null, "usage": {"input_tokens": 1152, "output_tokens": 339, "cache_read_input_tokens": 0, "cache_creation_input_tokens": 0}, "latency_ms": 2550.411249976605, "evaluated_at": "2026-09-09T21:59:27.602288+00:00"}
{"schema_version": "1.0", "prompt_version": "v2", "tool_uid": "AGI-is-going-to-arrive/Memory-Palace::create_memory::backend/mcp_server.py:4676", "repo": {"name_with_owner": "AGI-is-going-to-arrive/Memory-Palace", "stargazer_count": 311, "primary_language": "Python"}, "tool": {"name": "create_memory", "qualified_name": "create_memory", "description": "Creates a new memory under a parent URI.\n\n    Args:\n        parent_uri: Parent URI (e.g., \"core://agent\", \"writer://chapters\")\n                    Use \"core://\" or \"writer://\" for root level in that domain\n        content: Memory content\n        priority: **Retrieval Priority** (lower = higher priority, min 0).\n                    *   Priority controls retrieval ordering and conflict resolution.\n                    *   Compare it with the priorities of the currently visible memories.\n                    *   Ask: \"Where should this memory rank relative to the others I can see right now?\"\n                    *   Insert it between the memories that should be more and less preferred.\n        title: Optional title. If not provided, auto-assigns numeric ID\n        disclosure: A short trigger condition describing WHEN to read_memory() this node.\n                    Think: \"In what specific situation would I need to know this?\"\n\n    Returns:\n        The created memory's full URI\n\n    Examples:\n        create_memory(\"core://\", \"Bluesky usage rules...\", priority=2, title=\"bluesky_manual\", disclosure=\"When I prepare to browse Bluesky or check the timeline\")\n        create_memory(\"core://agent\", \"Love is more than just another program...\", priority=1, title=\"love_definition\", disclosure=\"When I start speaking like a tool or parasite\")"}, "scenario": "description_only", "judge": {"id": "gemini-3.5-flash-lite", "provider": "google", "model_id": "gemini-3.5-flash-lite", "raw_model_version": "gemini-3.5-flash-lite"}, "status": "ok", "scores": {"purpose": {"score": 5, "reasoning": "The description clearly explains that the tool creates a new memory under a specified parent URI, returning its full URI upon success."}, "guidelines": {"score": 4, "reasoning": "It provides strong operational and decision-making instructions regarding how to structure priorities and use the disclosure field, though explicit activation criteria for when to create versus update memories are brief."}, "limitations": {"score": 1, "reasoning": "There are no stated constraints, caveats, or failure modes mentioned (e.g., handling duplicate URIs or invalid domains)."}, "parameter_explanation": {"score": 5, "reasoning": "Every parameter (parent_uri, content, priority, title, disclosure) is thoroughly explained with semantic details, formatting examples, and conceptual guidance."}, "length_completeness": {"score": 5, "reasoning": "The description is substantial, spanning multiple well-formatted sections detailing arguments, return values, and behavior."}, "examples": {"score": 5, "reasoning": "It provides two clear and concrete code-like examples demonstrating correct usage with different parent URIs, priorities, titles, and disclosure conditions."}}, "error_detail": null, "source_code_sha256": null, "usage": {"input_tokens": 1108, "output_tokens": 313, "cache_read_input_tokens": 0, "cache_creation_input_tokens": 0}, "latency_ms": 4687.992084072903, "evaluated_at": "2026-09-09T21:59:29.754991+00:00"}
{"schema_version": "1.0", "prompt_version": "v2", "tool_uid": "AGI-is-going-to-arrive/Memory-Palace::read_memory::backend/mcp_server.py:4294", "repo": {"name_with_owner": "AGI-is-going-to-arrive/Memory-Palace", "stargazer_count": 311, "primary_language": "Python"}, "tool": {"name": "read_memory", "qualified_name": "read_memory", "description": "Reads a memory by its URI.\n\n    This is your primary mechanism for accessing memories.\n\n    Special System URIs:\n    - system://boot   : [Startup Only] Loads your core memories.\n    - system://index  : Loads a full index of all available memories.\n    - system://index-lite : Loads gist-backed lightweight index summary.\n    - system://audit  : Loads consolidated observability/audit summary.\n    - system://recent : Shows recently modified memories (default: 10).\n    - system://recent/N : Shows the N most recently modified memories (e.g. system://recent/20).\n\n    Note: Same Memory ID = same content (alias). Different ID + similar content = redundant content.\n\n    Args:\n        uri: The memory URI (e.g., \"core://memory-palace\", \"system://boot\")\n        chunk_id: Optional chunk index for partial reads (0-based).\n        range: Optional char range (`start:end` or `start-end`).\n        max_chars: Optional hard cap for returned characters.\n        include_ancestors: Optional parent-chain expansion for non-system URIs.\n\n    Returns:\n        - Default (no chunk/range/max_chars): legacy formatted memory text.\n        - Partial-read mode: structured JSON string with selection metadata.\n\n    Examples:\n        read_memory(\"core://agent\")\n        read_memory(\"core://agent/my_user\")\n        read_memory(\"writer://chapter_1/scene_1\")"}, "scenario": "with_source", "judge": {"id": "gemini-3.5-flash-lite", "provider": "google", "model_id": "gemini-3.5-flash-lite", "raw_model_version": "gemini-3.5-flash-lite"}, "status": "ok", "scores": {"purpose": {"score": 5, "reasoning": "The description clearly explains that the tool reads memories by URI and acts as the primary mechanism for accessing stored information, detailing special system URIs and fallback behavior."}, "guidelines": {"score": 4, "reasoning": "It specifies activation criteria (such as using system URIs for startup, index, or recent items) and operational instructions via argument descriptions, though operational guidance for partial-read modes is minimal."}, "limitations": {"score": 3, "reasoning": "It notes that the same memory ID represents an alias and different IDs with similar content mean redundancy, but it fails to mention technical constraints like error handling on invalid ranges or fallback behaviors shown in the code."}, "parameter_explanation": {"score": 4, "reasoning": "The arguments (uri, chunk_id, range, max_chars, include_ancestors) are described with clear data roles and examples, though subtle operational dependencies between them are left to the implementation."}, "length_completeness": {"score": 5, "reasoning": "The text is substantive and well-structured, containing multiple paragraphs, lists of system URIs, argument breakdowns, return descriptions, and usage examples."}, "examples": {"score": 4, "reasoning": "Three concrete usage examples are provided showing typical calls with different URIs, though examples demonstrating partial reads or system URIs would have made it ideal."}}, "error_detail": null, "source_code_sha256": "7aba3d3c96596c434e70f95cdcda9adbcec310361000cd9cb8dbebc270023af5", "usage": {"input_tokens": 10492, "output_tokens": 362, "cache_read_input_tokens": 0, "cache_creation_input_tokens": 0}, "latency_ms": 4764.071458019316, "evaluated_at": "2026-09-09T21:59:29.825246+00:00"}
{"schema_version": "1.0", "prompt_version": "v2", "tool_uid": "AGI-is-going-to-arrive/Memory-Palace::update_memory::backend/mcp_server.py:4925", "repo": {"name_with_owner": "AGI-is-going-to-arrive/Memory-Palace", "stargazer_count": 311, "primary_language": "Python"}, "tool": {"name": "update_memory", "qualified_name": "update_memory", "description": "Updates an existing memory to a new version.\n    The old version will be deleted.\n    Warning: read_memory first so you know exactly what you are overwriting.\n\n    Only provided fields are updated; others remain unchanged.\n\n    Two content-editing modes (mutually exclusive):\n\n    1. **Patch mode** (primary): Provide old_string + new_string.\n       Finds old_string in the existing content and replaces it with new_string.\n       old_string must match exactly ONE location in the content.\n       To delete a section, set new_string to empty string \"\".\n\n    2. **Append mode**: Provide append.\n       Adds the given text to the end of existing content.\n\n    There is NO full-replace mode. You must explicitly specify what you're changing\n    or removing via old_string/new_string. This prevents accidental content loss.\n\n    Args:\n        uri: URI to update (e.g., \"core://agent/my_user\")\n        old_string: [Patch mode] Text to find in existing content (must be unique)\n        new_string: [Patch mode] Text to replace old_string with. Use \"\" to delete a section.\n        append: [Append mode] Text to append to the end of existing content\n        priority: New priority (None = keep existing)\n        disclosure: New disclosure instruction (None = keep existing)\n\n    Returns:\n        Success message with URI\n\n    Examples:\n        update_memory(\"core://agent/my_user\", old_string=\"old paragraph content\", new_string=\"new paragraph content\")\n        update_memory(\"core://agent\", append=\"\\\\n## New Section\\\\nNew content...\")\n        update_memory(\"writer://chapter_1\", priority=5)"}, "scenario": "description_only", "judge": {"id": "gemini-3.5-flash-lite", "provider": "google", "model_id": "gemini-3.5-flash-lite", "raw_model_version": "gemini-3.5-flash-lite"}, "status": "ok", "scores": {"purpose": {"score": 5, "reasoning": "The description clearly explains that the tool updates an existing memory by either patching specific text or appending new content, deleting the old version in the process."}, "guidelines": {"score": 5, "reasoning": "It provides explicit operational instructions for the two mutually exclusive modes (Patch mode and Append mode) and gives a warning/activation criterion to read the memory first before overwriting."}, "limitations": {"score": 5, "reasoning": "It details key constraints such as the requirement that old_string must match exactly one location in the content, notes the lack of a full-replace mode to prevent accidental data loss, and warns about reading the memory first."}, "parameter_explanation": {"score": 5, "reasoning": "Each parameter (uri, old_string, new_string, append, priority, disclosure) is thoroughly explained with respect to its mode and behavior when omitted or set."}, "length_completeness": {"score": 5, "reasoning": "The description is detailed, well-structured with sections and bullet points, spanning well over three substantive sentences."}, "examples": {"score": 5, "reasoning": "It includes three clear and practical usage examples demonstrating patch mode, append mode, and updating metadata like priority."}}, "error_detail": null, "source_code_sha256": null, "usage": {"input_tokens": 1209, "output_tokens": 337, "cache_read_input_tokens": 0, "cache_creation_input_tokens": 0}, "latency_ms": 1891.2366658914834, "evaluated_at": "2026-09-09T21:59:31.646343+00:00"}
{"schema_version": "1.0", "prompt_version": "v2", "tool_uid": "AGI-is-going-to-arrive/Memory-Palace::create_memory::backend/mcp_server.py:4676", "repo": {"name_with_owner": "AGI-is-going-to-arrive/Memory-Palace", "stargazer_count": 311, "primary_language": "Python"}, "tool": {"name": "create_memory", "qualified_name": "create_memory", "description": "Creates a new memory under a parent URI.\n\n    Args:\n        parent_uri: Parent URI (e.g., \"core://agent\", \"writer://chapters\")\n                    Use \"core://\" or \"writer://\" for root level in that domain\n        content: Memory content\n        priority: **Retrieval Priority** (lower = higher priority, min 0).\n                    *   Priority controls retrieval ordering and conflict resolution.\n                    *   Compare it with the priorities of the currently visible memories.\n                    *   Ask: \"Where should this memory rank relative to the others I can see right now?\"\n                    *   Insert it between the memories that should be more and less preferred.\n        title: Optional title. If not provided, auto-assigns numeric ID\n        disclosure: A short trigger condition describing WHEN to read_memory() this node.\n                    Think: \"In what specific situation would I need to know this?\"\n\n    Returns:\n        The created memory's full URI\n\n    Examples:\n        create_memory(\"core://\", \"Bluesky usage rules...\", priority=2, title=\"bluesky_manual\", disclosure=\"When I prepare to browse Bluesky or check the timeline\")\n        create_memory(\"core://agent\", \"Love is more than just another program...\", priority=1, title=\"love_definition\", disclosure=\"When I start speaking like a tool or parasite\")"}, "scenario": "with_source", "judge": {"id": "gemini-3.5-flash-lite", "provider": "google", "model_id": "gemini-3.5-flash-lite", "raw_model_version": "gemini-3.5-flash-lite"}, "status": "ok", "scores": {"purpose": {"score": 5, "reasoning": "The description clearly and completely explains that the tool creates a new memory under a specified parent URI. It provides clear context on domain usage and expected outcomes."}, "guidelines": {"score": 4, "reasoning": "The description provides strong operational instructions and contextual decision-making criteria for parameters like priority and disclosure. However, it lacks explicit guidance regarding write guards or potential blocking conditions revealed in the source code."}, "limitations": {"score": 2, "reasoning": "The source code reveals constraints such as maximum character limits for content, strict regex validation requirements for titles (only Unicode letters, digits, underscores, or hyphens), and write guard blocking behavior, none of which are disclosed in the description."}, "parameter_explanation": {"score": 4, "reasoning": "Parameters like parent_uri, priority, title, and disclosure are explained thoroughly with semantic context. However, it fails to mention the technical constraints on the title format or content length validation implemented in the source code."}, "length_completeness": {"score": 5, "reasoning": "The description is substantial, spanning multiple sentences and paragraphs that detail arguments, return values, and concrete usage examples."}, "examples": {"score": 5, "reasoning": "Two clear and realistic illustrative examples are provided, demonstrating valid calls to the tool with different parameters."}}, "error_detail": null, "source_code_sha256": "ab310c806cb93cf505d974ab29c033533d12991fd6d9443ed81da057c24263a2", "usage": {"input_tokens": 9961, "output_tokens": 352, "cache_read_input_tokens": 0, "cache_creation_input_tokens": 0}, "latency_ms": 5863.401666050777, "evaluated_at": "2026-09-09T21:59:33.468393+00:00"}
{"schema_version": "1.0", "prompt_version": "v2", "tool_uid": "AGI-is-going-to-arrive/Memory-Palace::delete_memory::backend/mcp_server.py:5333", "repo": {"name_with_owner": "AGI-is-going-to-arrive/Memory-Palace", "stargazer_count": 311, "primary_language": "Python"}, "tool": {"name": "delete_memory", "qualified_name": "delete_memory", "description": "Delete a memory by removing its URI path.\n\n    Once a path is deleted, that route to the content is permanently gone.\n\n    Warning:\n    You are actively giving up access to part of the past. Read the current\n    content with read_memory before deleting it.\n\n\n    Args:\n        uri: The URI to delete (e.g., \"core://agent/old_note\")\n\n    Returns:\n        Success or error message\n\n    Examples:\n        delete_memory(\"core://agent/deprecated_belief\")\n        delete_memory(\"writer://draft_v1\")"}, "scenario": "with_source", "judge": {"id": "gemini-3.5-flash-lite", "provider": "google", "model_id": "gemini-3.5-flash-lite", "raw_model_version": "gemini-3.5-flash-lite"}, "status": "ok", "scores": {"purpose": {"score": 5, "reasoning": "The description clearly and completely explains that the tool deletes a memory by removing its URI path, stating that the route to the content is permanently gone."}, "guidelines": {"score": 4, "reasoning": "It offers clear operational instructions and includes a helpful warning advising the agent to read the content first with read_memory, though it lacks deeper activation criteria beyond general usage."}, "limitations": {"score": 3, "reasoning": "The description mentions that deletion is permanent and warns against losing past access, but it omits technical constraints revealed in the code such as domain restrictions (e.g., read-only domains like system://) and write-lane timeouts."}, "parameter_explanation": {"score": 3, "reasoning": "The uri parameter is explained with an example format (e.g., \"core://agent/old_note\"), but lacks detail on parsing behavior, legacy fallbacks, or domain requirements."}, "length_completeness": {"score": 4, "reasoning": "The description is substantive, spanning several paragraphs with a clear purpose, warning section, arguments list, return value description, and examples."}, "examples": {"score": 5, "reasoning": "Two clear, illustrative examples of correct usage are provided using different URI domains."}}, "error_detail": null, "source_code_sha256": "21327f07a422480c3cf8fc88b0088ceafb93ec8d70ad838a33d1a2cd646a014a", "usage": {"input_tokens": 10104, "output_tokens": 343, "cache_read_input_tokens": 0, "cache_creation_input_tokens": 0}, "latency_ms": 1914.9525419343263, "evaluated_at": "2026-09-09T21:59:35.380472+00:00"}
{"schema_version": "1.0", "prompt_version": "v2", "tool_uid": "AGI-is-going-to-arrive/Memory-Palace::update_memory::backend/mcp_server.py:4925", "repo": {"name_with_owner": "AGI-is-going-to-arrive/Memory-Palace", "stargazer_count": 311, "primary_language": "Python"}, "tool": {"name": "update_memory", "qualified_name": "update_memory", "description": "Updates an existing memory to a new version.\n    The old version will be deleted.\n    Warning: read_memory first so you know exactly what you are overwriting.\n\n    Only provided fields are updated; others remain unchanged.\n\n    Two content-editing modes (mutually exclusive):\n\n    1. **Patch mode** (primary): Provide old_string + new_string.\n       Finds old_string in the existing content and replaces it with new_string.\n       old_string must match exactly ONE location in the content.\n       To delete a section, set new_string to empty string \"\".\n\n    2. **Append mode**: Provide append.\n       Adds the given text to the end of existing content.\n\n    There is NO full-replace mode. You must explicitly specify what you're changing\n    or removing via old_string/new_string. This prevents accidental content loss.\n\n    Args:\n        uri: URI to update (e.g., \"core://agent/my_user\")\n        old_string: [Patch mode] Text to find in existing content (must be unique)\n        new_string: [Patch mode] Text to replace old_string with. Use \"\" to delete a section.\n        append: [Append mode] Text to append to the end of existing content\n        priority: New priority (None = keep existing)\n        disclosure: New disclosure instruction (None = keep existing)\n\n    Returns:\n        Success message with URI\n\n    Examples:\n        update_memory(\"core://agent/my_user\", old_string=\"old paragraph content\", new_string=\"new paragraph content\")\n        update_memory(\"core://agent\", append=\"\\\\n## New Section\\\\nNew content...\")\n        update_memory(\"writer://chapter_1\", priority=5)"}, "scenario": "with_source", "judge": {"id": "gemini-3.5-flash-lite", "provider": "google", "model_id": "gemini-3.5-flash-lite", "raw_model_version": "gemini-3.5-flash-lite"}, "status": "ok", "scores": {"purpose": {"score": 5, "reasoning": "The description clearly explains that the tool updates an existing memory by providing editing modes (patch and append) or metadata adjustments. The source code confirms that it handles these mutually exclusive modes and performs updates matching the description."}, "guidelines": {"score": 5, "reasoning": "The description provides explicit operational instructions regarding the mutually exclusive patch and append modes, and warns the user to call read_memory first. The source code enforces these rules by returning errors if both modes are used or if requirements like unique old_string matching are violated."}, "limitations": {"score": 4, "reasoning": "The description explicitly warns that old_string must match exactly one location and that there is no full-replace mode. The source code reveals additional validation checks such as max character limits and write guard blocking, which are minor technical details not fully enumerated but well-captured by the general constraints."}, "parameter_explanation": {"score": 5, "reasoning": "Each parameter's role, context, and mode dependency (such as [Patch mode] or [Append mode]) are thoroughly explained. The source code correctly validates these exact parameters according to their documented semantics."}, "length_completeness": {"score": 5, "reasoning": "The description is extensive, spanning multiple structured paragraphs, sections for modes, arguments, return values, and concrete examples. It provides deep substantive detail suitable for an LLM agent."}, "examples": {"score": 5, "reasoning": "The description includes three distinct and accurate examples illustrating patch mode, append mode, and metadata updating. These examples directly match the tool's signature and implementation behavior."}}, "error_detail": null, "source_code_sha256": "56b33a86d0c5f15b10e1e5211da95145abeb4719d8355c60d6bab3037ea07d18", "usage": {"input_tokens": 9566, "output_tokens": 413, "cache_read_input_tokens": 0, "cache_creation_input_tokens": 0}, "latency_ms": 5577.678583096713, "evaluated_at": "2026-09-09T21:59:35.401338+00:00"}
{"schema_version": "1.0", "prompt_version": "v2", "tool_uid": "AGI-is-going-to-arrive/Memory-Palace::add_alias::backend/mcp_server.py:5441", "repo": {"name_with_owner": "AGI-is-going-to-arrive/Memory-Palace", "stargazer_count": 311, "primary_language": "Python"}, "tool": {"name": "add_alias", "qualified_name": "add_alias", "description": "Creates an alias URI pointing to the same memory as target_uri.\n\n    Use this to increase a memory's reachability via multiple URIs.\n    Aliases can even cross domains (e.g., link a writer draft to a core memory).\n\n    Args:\n        new_uri: New URI to create (alias)\n        target_uri: Existing URI to alias\n        priority: Retrieval priority for this specific alias context (lower = higher priority). This controls retrieval ordering for the alias.\n        disclosure: Disclosure condition for this specific alias context\n\n    Returns:\n        Success message\n\n    Examples:\n        add_alias(\"core://timeline/2024/05/20\", \"core://agent/my_user/first_meeting\", priority=1, disclosure=\"When I want to know how we start\")"}, "scenario": "description_only", "judge": {"id": "gemini-3.5-flash-lite", "provider": "google", "model_id": "gemini-3.5-flash-lite", "raw_model_version": "gemini-3.5-flash-lite"}, "status": "ok", "scores": {"purpose": {"score": 5, "reasoning": "The description clearly explains that the tool creates an alias URI pointing to an existing memory, helping increase reachability across domains."}, "guidelines": {"score": 3, "reasoning": "It specifies when to use the tool (to increase reachability or link drafts to core memories), but lacks thorough operational instructions on how parameters like disclosure interact."}, "limitations": {"score": 1, "reasoning": "There is no mention of constraints, potential failure modes (such as target URI not existing or URI collision), or edge cases."}, "parameter_explanation": {"score": 4, "reasoning": "Parameters like new_uri, target_uri, priority (explaining lower equals higher priority), and disclosure are well described in terms of their roles."}, "length_completeness": {"score": 4, "reasoning": "The description spans multiple substantive sections including purpose, argument definitions, return type, and an example, making it comprehensive."}, "examples": {"score": 5, "reasoning": "A clear, concrete usage example is provided showing how to call the function with appropriate arguments."}}, "error_detail": null, "source_code_sha256": null, "usage": {"input_tokens": 984, "output_tokens": 305, "cache_read_input_tokens": 0, "cache_creation_input_tokens": 0}, "latency_ms": 1647.8964160196483, "evaluated_at": "2026-09-09T21:59:37.028745+00:00"}
