{"schema_version": "1.0", "prompt_version": "v2", "tool_uid": "Accenture/mcp-bench::qr_decompose::mcp_servers/scientific_computation_mcp/src/linear_algebra.py:224", "repo": {"name_with_owner": "Accenture/mcp-bench", "stargazer_count": 502, "primary_language": "Python"}, "tool": {"name": "qr_decompose", "qualified_name": "qr_decompose", "description": "Computes the QR decomposition of a stored matrix.\n\n        Decomposes the matrix A into A = Q @ R, where Q is an orthogonal matrix\n        and R is an upper triangular matrix.\n\n        Args:\n            name (str): The name of the matrix to decompose.\n\n        Returns:\n            dict: A dictionary with keys:\n                - 'q': np.ndarray, the orthogonal matrix Q\n                - 'r': np.ndarray, the upper triangular matrix R\n\n        Raises:\n            ValueError: If the matrix is not found or decomposition fails."}, "scenario": "description_only", "judge": {"id": "gemini-3.5-flash-lite", "provider": "google", "model_id": "gemini-3.5-flash-lite", "raw_model_version": null}, "status": "error", "scores": null, "error_detail": "gemini API error 429: You exceeded your current quota, please check your plan and billing details. For more information on this error, head to: https://ai.google.dev/gemini-api/docs/rate-limits. To monitor your current usage, head to: https://ai.dev/rate-limit. \n* Quota exceeded for metric: generativelanguage.googleapis.com/generate_content_free_tier_requests, limit: 15, model: gemini-3.5-flash-lite\nPlease retry in 12.820357197s.", "source_code_sha256": null, "usage": null, "latency_ms": null, "evaluated_at": "2026-09-09T22:02:47.257526+00:00"}
{"schema_version": "1.0", "prompt_version": "v2", "tool_uid": "Accenture/mcp-bench::svd_decompose::mcp_servers/scientific_computation_mcp/src/linear_algebra.py:253", "repo": {"name_with_owner": "Accenture/mcp-bench", "stargazer_count": 502, "primary_language": "Python"}, "tool": {"name": "svd_decompose", "qualified_name": "svd_decompose", "description": "Computes the Singular Value Decomposition (SVD) of a stored matrix.\n\n        Decomposes the matrix A into A = U @ S @ V^T, where U and V^T are orthogonal\n        matrices, and S is a diagonal matrix of singular values.\n\n        Args:\n            name (str): The name of the matrix to decompose.\n\n        Returns:\n            dict: A dictionary with keys:\n                - 'u': np.ndarray, the left singular vectors\n                - 's': np.ndarray, the singular values\n                - 'v_t': np.ndarray, the right singular vectors transposed\n\n        Raises:\n            ValueError: If the matrix is not found or decomposition fails."}, "scenario": "with_source", "judge": {"id": "gemini-3.5-flash-lite", "provider": "google", "model_id": "gemini-3.5-flash-lite", "raw_model_version": "gemini-3.5-flash-lite"}, "status": "ok", "scores": {"purpose": {"score": 5, "reasoning": "The description clearly explains that the tool computes the Singular Value Decomposition of a stored matrix into its components U, S, and V^T."}, "guidelines": {"score": 2, "reasoning": "The description mentions the function and expected input/output, but lacks explicit decision-making activation criteria or usage guidelines beyond basic syntax."}, "limitations": {"score": 4, "reasoning": "It documents that a ValueError is raised if the matrix is not found or if the decomposition fails, matching the source code behavior accurately."}, "parameter_explanation": {"score": 4, "reasoning": "The parameter 'name' is described as the name of the matrix to decompose, which is clear and maps directly to the store lookup in the source code."}, "length_completeness": {"score": 4, "reasoning": "The description is substantive, covering purpose, arguments, return structure, and exceptions across multiple well-formatted lines."}, "examples": {"score": 1, "reasoning": "No concrete examples of correct and effective usage are provided in the description."}}, "error_detail": null, "source_code_sha256": "baefb3dfb5f4b79d7852e60a6a2c1e250c1b7cff7fdbf6438b9a35c2198fb2c1", "usage": {"input_tokens": 1382, "output_tokens": 301, "cache_read_input_tokens": 0, "cache_creation_input_tokens": 0}, "latency_ms": 4017.9762500338256, "evaluated_at": "2026-09-09T22:02:51.275445+00:00"}
