 could be added."}, "length_completeness": {"score": 3, "reasoning": "The text provides structured parameter documentation reaching a moderate level of completeness, but is presented mostly as a raw docstring fragment rather than full prose."}, "examples": {"score": 1, "reasoning": "No illustrative examples of correct and effective usage are provided in the description."}}, "error_detail": null, "source_code_sha256": null, "usage": {"input_tokens": 989, "output_tokens": 289, "cache_read_input_tokens": 0, "cache_creation_input_tokens": 0}, "latency_ms": 1809.7195408772677, "evaluated_at": "2026-09-09T22:16:14.924823+00:00"}
{"schema_version": "1.0", "prompt_version": "v2", "tool_uid": "Accenture/mcp-bench::prevent_cvd_risk::mcp_servers/medcalc/medcalc/calculator.py:1282", "repo": {"name_with_owner": "Accenture/mcp-bench", "stargazer_count": 502, "primary_language": "Python"}, "tool": {"name": "prevent_cvd_risk", "qualified_name": "prevent_cvd_risk", "description": "Predicting Risk of Cardiovascular Disease EVENTs (PREVENT)\n    Predicts 10-year risk of CVD in patients aged 30-79 without known CVD.\n    \n    Parameters:\n    -----------\n    age : int\n        Age in years (30-79)\n    female : bool\n        True if patient is female, False if male\n    tc : float\n        Total cholesterol in mmol/L\n    hdl : float\n        HDL cholesterol in mmol/L\n    sbp : int\n        Systolic blood pressure in mmHg\n    diabetes : bool\n        True if patient has diabetes\n    current_smoker : bool\n        True if patient is a current smoker\n    egfr : float\n        Estimated glomerular filtration rate in mL/min/1.73m²\n    using_antihtn : bool\n        True if patient is using antihypertensive drugs\n    using_statins : bool\n        True if patient is using statins\n    \n    Returns:\n    --------\n    float\n        10-year CVD risk as a percentage"}, "scenario": "description_only", "judge": {"id": "gemini-3.5-flash-lite", "provider": "google", "model_id": "gemini-3.5-flash-lite", "raw_model_version": "gemini-3.5-flash-lite"}, "status": "ok", "scores": {"purpose": {"score": 5, "reasoning": "The description clearly explains that the tool predicts the 10-year risk of cardiovascular disease (CVD) events using the PREVENT model for specific patient demographics."}, "guidelines": {"score": 2, "reasoning": "It specifies activation criteria by mentioning the target population (patients aged 30-79 without known CVD), but lacks operational instructions or decision-making guidance on how or when to invoke it."}, "limitations": {"score": 2, "reasoning": "The description implies an age boundary (30-79) and population constraint (without known CVD), but fails to explicitly discuss other clinical failure modes, validity caveats, or missing data constraints."}, "parameter_explanation": {"score": 4, "reasoning": "Parameters are defined with their expected types, units (e.g., mmol/L, mmHg, mL/min/1.73m²), and semantic roles, though minor additional detail on value boundaries (beyond age) could improve it."}, "length_completeness": {"score": 4, "reasoning": "The description provides substantial detail spanning multiple lines covering purpose, parameters, and return types, easily clearing the length threshold."}, "examples": {"score": 1, "reasoning": "No examples of correct usage or sample invocations are provided within the description."}}, "error_detail": null, "source_code_sha256": null, "usage": {"input_tokens": 1046, "output_tokens": 353, "cache_read_input_tokens": 0, "cache_creation_input_tokens": 0}, "latency_ms": 1963.3261668495834, "evaluated_at": "2026-09-09T22:16:20.080405+00:00"}
{"schema_version": "1.0", "prompt_version": "v2", "tool_uid": "Accenture/mcp-bench::prevent_cvd_risk::mcp_servers/medcalc/medcalc/calculator.py:1282", "repo": {"name_with_owner": "Accenture/mcp-bench", "stargazer_count": 502, "primary_language": "Python"}, "tool": {"name": "prevent_cvd_risk", "qualified_name": "prevent_cvd_risk", "description": "Predicting Risk of Cardiovascular Disease EVENTs (PREVENT)\n    Predicts 10-year risk of CVD in patients aged 30-79 without known CVD.\n    \n    Parameters:\n    -----------\n    age : int\n        Age in years (30-79)\n    female : bool\n        True if patient is female, False if male\n    tc : float\n        Total cholesterol in mmol/L\n    hdl : float\n        HDL cholesterol in mmol/L\n    sbp : int\n        Systolic blood pressure in mmHg\n    diabetes : bool\n        True if patient has diabetes\n    current_smoker : bool\n        True if patient is a current smoker\n    egfr : float\n        Estimated glomerular filtration rate in mL/min/1.73m²\n    using_antihtn : bool\n        True if patient is using antihypertensive drugs\n    using_statins : bool\n        True if patient is using statins\n    \n    Returns:\n    --------\n    float\n        10-year CVD risk as a percentage"}, "scenario": "with_source", "judge": {"id": "gemini-3.5-flash-lite", "provider": "google", "model_id": "gemini-3.5-flash-lite", "raw_model_version": "gemini-3.5-flash-lite"}, "status": "ok", "scores": {"purpose": {"score": 5, "reasoning": "The description clearly explains that the tool predicts the 10-year risk of cardiovascular disease using the PREVENT model for patients aged 30-79. It aligns accurately with the source code implementation."}, "guidelines": {"score": 3, "reasoning": "The description specifies activation criteria based on patient age (30-79) and disease history, but lacks operational instructions on when or how an agent should invoke the tool within a broader workflow."}, "limitations": {"score": 2, "reasoning": "The description mentions age constraints (30-79) and lack of known CVD, but fails to document the strict ValueError exception raised by the code if age falls outside this range, or any missing parameter edge cases."}, "parameter_explanation": {"score": 4, "reasoning": "Parameters are clearly listed with their expected data types and units/ranges (e.g., age in years, total cholesterol in mmol/L). However, it does not detail internal transformations or boolean flags beyond basic descriptions."}, "length_completeness": {"score": 4, "reasoning": "The description is thorough, structured, and spans multiple lines detailing purpose, parameters, and return type, making it easy to read despite lacking examples."}, "examples": {"score": 1, "reasoning": "No illustrative examples of usage or expected outputs are provided in the description."}}, "error_detail": null, "source_code_sha256": "6f92704a89302514c2f86004859868e10f44cb3f37cd8c5c409f4e471f84ec0d", "usage": {"input_tokens": 3563, "output_tokens": 366, "cache_read_input_tokens": 0, "cache_creation_input_tokens": 0}, "latency_ms": 5037.42870897986, "evaluated_at": "2026-09-09T22:16:28.154446+00:00"}
{"schema_version": "1.0", "prompt_version": "v2", "tool_uid": "Accenture/mcp-bench::corrected_calcium::mcp_servers/medcalc/medcalc/calculator.py:1437", "repo": {"name_with_owner": "Accenture/mcp-bench", "stargazer_count": 502, "primary_language": "Python"}, "tool": {"name": "corrected_calcium", "qualified_name": "corrected_calcium", "description": "Calcium Correction for Hypoalbuminemia and Hyperalbuminemia\n    Calculates a corrected calcium level for patients with abnormal albumin levels.\n    \n    Parameters:\n    -----------\n    serum_calcium : float\n        Patient's measured serum calcium level in mg/dL\n    patient_albumin : float\n        Patient's serum albumin level in g/dL\n    normal_albumin : float, optional\n        Normal/reference albumin level in g/dL, default is 4.0 g/dL\n    \n    Returns:\n    --------\n    float\n        Corrected calcium level in mg/dL\n        \n    Formula:\n    --------\n    Corrected Calcium = (0.8 * (Normal Albumin - Patient's Albumin)) + Serum Calcium\n    \n    References:\n    -----------\n    Payne RB, et al. Br Med J. 1973;4(5893):643-646."}, "scenario": "description_only", "judge": {"id": "gemini-3.5-flash-lite", "provider": "google", "model_id": "gemini-3.5-flash-lite", "raw_model_version": "gemini-3.5-flash-lite"}, "status": "ok", "scores": {"purpose": {"score": 5, "reasoning": "The description clearly explains that the tool calculates a corrected calcium level for patients with abnormal albumin levels using established medical formulas."}, "guidelines": {"score": 1, "reasoning": "The description provides no operational activation criteria or guidance on when to use this tool versus other potential calculations."}, "limitations": {"score": 1, "reasoning": "There is no mention of constraints, edge cases, or failure modes (e.g., handling negative or zero albumin values)."}, "parameter_explanation": {"score": 4, "reasoning": "The parameters serum_calcium, patient_albumin, and normal_albumin are clearly explained along with their units and default values."}, "length_completeness": {"score": 4, "reasoning": "The text spans multiple substantive sections including parameters, returns, formula, and references, making it quite complete for a clinical calculation tool."}, "examples": {"score": 1, "reasoning": "No concrete usage examples with sample inputs and expected outputs are provided."}}, "error_detail": null, "source_code_sha256": null, "usage": {"input_tokens": 1011, "output_tokens": 287, "cache_read_input_tokens": 0, "cache_creation_input_tokens": 0}, "latency_ms": 5231.377250049263, "evaluated_at": "2026-09-09T22:16:33.350416+00:00"}
{"schema_version": "1.0", "prompt_version": "v2", "tool_uid": "Accenture/mcp-bench::corrected_calcium::mcp_servers/medcalc/medcalc/calculator.py:1437", "repo": {"name_with_owner": "Accenture/mcp-bench", "stargazer_count": 502, "primary_language": "Python"}, "tool": {"name": "corrected_calcium", "qualified_name": "corrected_calcium", "description": "Calcium Correction for Hypoalbuminemia and Hyperalbuminemia\n    Calculates a corrected calcium level for patients with abnormal albumin levels.\n    \n    Parameters:\n    -----------\n    serum_calcium : float\n        Patient's measured serum calcium level in mg/dL\n    patient_albumin : float\n        Patient's serum albumin level in g/dL\n    normal_albumin : float, optional\n        Normal/reference albumin level in g/dL, default is 4.0 g/dL\n    \n    Returns:\n    --------\n    float\n        Corrected calcium level in mg/dL\n        \n    Formula:\n    --------\n    Corrected Calcium = (0.8 * (Normal Albumin - Patient's Albumin)) + Serum Calcium\n    \n    References:\n    -----------\n    Payne RB, et al. Br Med J. 1973;4(5893):643-646."}, "scenario": "with_source", "judge": {"id": "gemini-3.5-flash-lite", "provider": "google", "model_id": "gemini-3.5-flash-lite", "raw_model_version": "gemini-3.5-flash-lite"}, "status": "ok", "scores": {"purpose": {"score": 5, "reasoning": "The description clearly and completely explains that the tool calculates a corrected calcium level for patients with abnormal albumin levels. It provides the exact medical formula used and references the original study."}, "guidelines": {"score": 2, "reasoning": "The description states what the tool calculates and lists parameters, but lacks explicit operational instructions or activation criteria guiding when an LLM should apply this specific calculation versus others."}, "limitations": {"score": 1, "reasoning": "The description fails to mention any input validation constraints or exceptions present in the source code, such as requiring posi