{"schema_version": "1.0", "prompt_version": "v2", "tool_uid": "Accenture/mcp-bench::qtc_calculator::mcp_servers/medcalc/medcalc/calculator.py:1503", "repo": {"name_with_owner": "Accenture/mcp-bench", "stargazer_count": 502, "primary_language": "Python"}, "tool": {"name": "qtc_calculator", "qualified_name": "qtc_calculator", "description": "Corrected QT Interval (QTc) Calculator\n    Corrects the QT interval for heart rate extremes using various formulas.\n    \n    Parameters:\n    -----------\n    qt_interval : float\n        Measured QT interval in milliseconds (ms)\n    heart_rate : float\n        Heart rate in beats per minute (bpm)\n    formula : str, optional\n        Formula to use for correction (default: \"bazett\")\n        Options: \"bazett\", \"fridericia\", \"framingham\", \"hodges\", \"rautaharju\"\n    \n    Returns:\n    --------\n    qtc : float\n        Corrected QT interval in milliseconds (ms)\n        \n    Formulas:\n    ---------\n    RR interval = 60 / heart_rate (in seconds)\n    Bazett: QTc = QT / √(RR)\n    Fridericia: QTc = QT / (RR)^(1/3)\n    Framingham: QTc = QT + 154 × (1 - RR)\n    Hodges: QTc = QT + 1.75 × (heart_rate - 60)\n    Rautaharju: QTc = QT × (120 + heart_rate) / 180\n    \n    References:\n    -----------\n    Bazett HC. Heart. 1920;7:353-370\n    Fridericia LS. Acta Med Scand. 1920;53:469-486\n    Sagie A, et al. Am J Cardiol. 1992;70(7):797-801 (Framingham)\n    Hodges M, et al. J Electrocardiol. 1983;16(1):17-24\n    Rautaharju PM, et al. J Am Coll Cardiol. 2004;44(3):594-600"}, "scenario": "with_source", "judge": {"id": "gemini-3.5-flash-lite", "provider": "google", "model_id": "gemini-3.5-flash-lite", "raw_model_version": "gemini-3.5-flash-lite"}, "status": "ok", "scores": {"purpose": {"score": 5, "reasoning": "The description clearly explains that the tool calculates the Corrected QT Interval (QTc) using various formulas based on measured QT interval and heart rate."}, "guidelines": {"score": 3, "reasoning": "The description lists available options and formulas, but provides minimal operational guidelines or decision-making criteria regarding when to invoke the tool."}, "limitations": {"score": 2, "reasoning": "The description lacks explicit discussion of edge cases, errors, or constraints, though the source code reveals interpretation logic (e.g., normal ranges, risks) that is entirely omitted from the description."}, "parameter_explanation": {"score": 4, "reasoning": "The input parameters qt_interval, heart_rate, and formula are well-defined with types, units, and available options."}, "length_completeness": {"score": 5, "reasoning": "The description is thorough, structured with multiple sections including parameters, returned values, formulas, and references, easily exceeding three to four substantive sentences."}, "examples": {"score": 1, "reasoning": "No concrete usage examples or input/output illustrations are provided in the description."}}, "error_detail": null, "source_code_sha256": "1da7a3d456d2c5ff0414c2d95e843155abfe96a0552bf0153ef7caf6050c266d", "usage": {"input_tokens": 2768, "output_tokens": 316, "cache_read_input_tokens": 0, "cache_creation_input_tokens": 0}, "latency_ms": 23412.158582825214, "evaluated_at": "2026-09-09T22:17:06.527765+00:00"}
