ompleteness without reaching three to four substantive sentences."}, "examples": {"score": 1, "reasoning": "No illustrative examples of correct or effective usage are provided in the description."}}, "error_detail": null, "source_code_sha256": null, "usage": {"input_tokens": 872, "output_tokens": 327, "cache_read_input_tokens": 0, "cache_creation_input_tokens": 0}, "latency_ms": 9733.335167169571, "evaluated_at": "2026-09-09T22:17:07.852968+00:00"}
{"schema_version": "1.0", "prompt_version": "v2", "tool_uid": "Accenture/mcp-bench::ibw_calculator::mcp_servers/medcalc/medcalc/calculator.py:1746", "repo": {"name_with_owner": "Accenture/mcp-bench", "stargazer_count": 502, "primary_language": "Python"}, "tool": {"name": "ibw_calculator", "qualified_name": "ibw_calculator", "description": "Ideal Body Weight and Adjusted Body Weight Calculator\n    Calculates ideal body weight (Devine formula) and adjusted body weight.\n    \n    Parameters:\n    -----------\n    weight_kg : float\n        Actual body weight in kilograms\n    height_inches : float\n        Height in inches\n    male : bool\n        True if patient is male, False if female\n    \n    Returns:\n    --------\n    ibw: float\n        Ideal body weight in kilograms\n        \n    Formulas:\n    ---------\n    Ideal Body Weight (IBW) (Devine formula):\n    - Men: IBW = 50 kg + 2.3 kg × (height in inches - 60)\n    - Women: IBW = 45.5 kg + 2.3 kg × (height in inches - 60)\n    \n    Adjusted Body Weight (ABW):\n    - ABW = IBW + 0.4 × (actual weight - IBW)\n    \n    References:\n    -----------\n    Devine BJ. Gentamicin therapy. Drug Intell Clin Pharm. 1974;8:650-655.\n    Pai MP. Drug Dosing Based on Weight and Body Surface Area: Mathematical Assumptions and Limitations in Obese Adults. Pharmacotherapy. 2012;32(9):856-868."}, "scenario": "description_only", "judge": {"id": "gemini-3.5-flash-lite", "provider": "google", "model_id": "gemini-3.5-flash-lite", "raw_model_version": "gemini-3.5-flash-lite"}, "status": "ok", "scores": {"purpose": {"score": 5, "reasoning": "The description clearly explains that the tool calculates ideal body weight using the Devine formula and adjusted body weight based on height, weight, and sex."}, "guidelines": {"score": 2, "reasoning": "The description states what the tool calculates and lists the exact formulas used, but lacks operational instructions or decision-making criteria on when specifically to use the tool versus other dosing weights."}, "limitations": {"score": 1, "reasoning": "There are no known constraints, caveats, error conditions, or failure modes mentioned in the description."}, "parameter_explanation": {"score": 4, "reasoning": "The input parameters (weight_kg, height_inches, male) are clearly explained with their expected units and data types, though minor edge cases like handling heights under 60 inches are not elaborated."}, "length_completeness": {"score": 4, "reasoning": "The description provides comprehensive details including parameters, return values, mathematical formulas, and literature references, spanning well past the minimum length requirement."}, "examples": {"score": 1, "reasoning": "The description provides no illustrative examples of correct or effective usage showing sample inputs and expected outputs."}}, "error_detail": null, "source_code_sha256": null, "usage": {"input_tokens": 1107, "output_tokens": 322, "cache_read_input_tokens": 0, "cache_creation_input_tokens": 0}, "latency_ms": 1899.7570830397308, "evaluated_at": "2026-09-09T22:17:10.016460+00:00"}
